 "narrative": "All returned estimates and intervals are already signed to the claimed hypothesis direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has lower outcome_001, i.e. stronger composite dependency. For direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has higher outcome_001, i.e. weaker composite dependency. The scientific threshold is 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction, and I used the rule that acceptance requires the signed point estimate and the credible lower-bound evidence to support an effect at least that large. H180 and H183 are accepted and closed. H180 tests feature_010 positive versus negative in the feature_063-negative complement and gives +0.402 with lower bound +0.300. H183 tests feature_002 positive versus negative in the same feature_063-negative complement and gives +0.863 with lower bound +0.796. Both are large, directionally clear, and have adequate cell sizes. They support the dataset-specific conclusions that feature_010 and feature_002 are associated with higher outcome_001 independently of samples in which feature_063 is positive, but they do not adjust for other correlated predictors. H189 is accepted and closed: feature_027 positive versus negative in feature_037-negative samples gives +0.817 with lower bound +0.693. H190 is accepted but kept active: feature_027 positive versus negative in feature_037-positive samples gives +0.635 with lower bound +0.448. The direction and size are strongly supportive, but the exposed cell has only 29 observations and feature_027 is rare and correlated with other accepted predictors, so I treat this as a strong rare-cell dataset-specific localization rather than a precisely established uniform stratum effect. H200 is rejected and closed. The feature_063 contrast in feature_018-positive samples is signed negative (-0.101) with an interval crossing zero. There is no meaningful support for the claimed lower-outcome direction in that stratum, and the imprecision does not justify a firm opposite claim beyond this sample. H201 is accepted and closed: feature_063 positive versus negative in feature_018-negative signature samples gives +0.359 with lower bound +0.183, which clears the threshold and supports the context-dependent feature_063 lower-outcome association. H257 is accepted and closed: in a higher-feature_040, overlap-reduced core with feature_002, feature_027, and feature_010 negative, feature_063 positive versus negative gives +0.383 with lower bound +0.221. This strengthens the feature_063 lower-outcome map in an adequately populated cleaned context. H258 is left unresolved and deferred rather than rejected. In the analogous lower-feature_040 cleaned core, feature_063 gives +0.234, but the lower bound is +0.126, below the 0.15 threshold. The interval excludes zero and is directionally consistent, so this supports the broader feature_063 association but does not credibly establish threshold-level precision in that specific stratum. H253 and H254 are accepted. H253 tests feature_010 in higher-feature_040 double signature-negative samples and gives +0.794 with lower bound +0.546; it is accepted but kept active because the exposed cell has only 29 observations, so rare-cell robustness remains a concern. H254 tests feature_010 in lower-feature_040 double signature-negative samples and gives +0.850 with lower bound +0.721; it is accepted and closed. These results sharpen the feature_010 context map: the weaker-dependency or higher-outcome association is large in signature-negative contexts across feature_040 strata. H263 and H264 are accepted and closed. Feature_037 positive versus negative in lower-feature_040 and higher-feature_040 cores that exclude feature_010, feature_063, and feature_027 gives +0.820 with lower bound +0.757 and +0.832 with lower bound +0.747 respectively. These are very strong threshold-clearing associations and support robustness of the feature_037 lower-outcome marker in cleaner contexts. Critically, these are marginal single-predictor contrasts conditional on eligibility and subgroup filters, not adjusted causal effects. The many subgroup tests raise multiplicity concerns, but I accepted only contrasts whose point estimates and lower bounds are far above the threshold, with the exception of rare-cell caveats for feature_027 and the high-PFS double-signature feature_010 cell. Marginal feature_063 strata remain unresolved rather than rejected. No validation request is made because independent validation quota is exhausted; all conclusions remain discovery-dataset-specific.",
 "research_notes": "Validation is exhausted. Current dataset-specific association map: feature_037 positive is a robust lower-outcome / stronger-dependency marker; strongest and threshold-clearing overall and in clean feature_010-negative, feature_063-negative, feature_027-negative high and low feature_040 cores. feature_002 positive is a robust higher-outcome / weaker-dependency marker; validated and persistent in feature_063-negative cores. feature_010 positive is associated with higher outcome_001 overall and in feature_063-negative cores, with large threshold-clearing effects in double feature_038- and feature_018-negative high and low feature_040 contexts; it remains attenuated or weak in signature-positive contexts. The high feature_040 double signature-negative feature_010 core is accepted but small exposed cell, so interpret cautiously. feature_027 positive is a very strong lower-outcome marker but rare; accepted in feature_037-negative and feature_037-positive contexts, with active caution in the feature_037-positive rare cell. feature_063 positive is a credible modest lower-outcome marker, stronger in feature_018-negative and high feature_040 cleaned cores, but some lower feature_040 cleaned strata are directionally supportive yet below threshold-precision: H258 estimate +0.234 lower +0.126 is unresolved. feature_018-positive feature_063 stratum H200 is rejected because signed effect is negative and interval crosses zero; this supports signature context dependence for feature_063 but not a firm opposite effect. Null or unsupported: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 main effects and tested marker interactions; feature_031 after failed validation; feature_024 after validation; feature_046 main below threshold; many broad screens null or underpowered. Decision rule: accept only when signed point and interval lower bound exceed 0.15 in the claimed direction; accept rare small-cell results with explicit caution. Next analysis should use active untested and newly proposed precision/context comparisons: feature_063 in broader feature_018-negative cleaned cores, feature_063 in lower feature_040 feature_018-negative cleaned cores, feature_010 in lower feature_040 double signature-negative feature_027- and feature_063-negative cores, plus remaining active feature_010 double-signature clean high feature_040 comparisons. No further independent validation can be requested. All conclusions remain dataset-specific, non-causal, non-adjusted, and not externally generalizable."
